---
description: Standards for x402 backend integration and the Coinbase CDP SDK
globs: src/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---
- Always use Node.js and TypeScript for backend routing.
- Use `@coinbase/cdp-sdk` for Bazaar discovery, CDP wallets, and `CdpX402Client` payment signing.
- Use `wrapFetchWithPayment` from `@x402/fetch` (not the older `x402-fetch` package name) to handle HTTP 402 automatically.
- Do not manually construct HTTP 402 retry loops; rely on SDK helpers.
- Drive network selection via `X402_ENV` in `src/config.ts` (`development` = Base Sepolia, `production` = Base mainnet). Never hardcode only Sepolia in new code.
- Outbound payments: Treasury signs via CDP and pays upstream Bazaar sellers; collect markup with Treasury → Merchant USDC transfer (needs a little ETH on Base for gas).
- Inbound paywall (V6): callers should pay x402dispatcher first; then the proxy settles upstream from Treasury/Merchant float.
- Prefer `eip155:8453` / `eip155:84532` CAIP-2 network ids when filtering Bazaar accepts.
- Reference canonical examples from Coinbase CDP x402 docs rather than guessing implementations.
